{"binding":{"contracts":"sha256:1df0afc21301595b72a5f9bdad3ab2aade7452ad1c5a4f97455bde354bf1120a","parser":"sha256:97d6893eb291808dc0f0cc19b90d6fdbe13cafd37c4319cc9e0c7a2bdafb7485","policy":"planning-facts/1"},"exitCode":0,"facts":{"acceptance":[{"id":"AC1","line":25,"text":"Regression verdict. Run on a repository with Habit Hooks configured, gatereeve code-health --base <ref> (and the plugin-local node <plugin-root>/resources/code-health/cli.js --base <ref>) does the following:"},{"id":"AC2","line":41,"text":"UNAVAILABLE conditions. The wrapper reports UNAVAILABLE with a message naming the cause and the way forward when any of these holds:"},{"id":"AC3","line":46,"text":"Core enforcement. In a run started under this version, a PR-boundary review round doesn't qualify unless its consumed Verification contains a PASS code-health receipt for the candidate tree."},{"id":"AC4","line":52,"text":"Human decisions."},{"id":"AC5","line":58,"text":"CI coverage. The acceptance milestone treats a converged review's consumed code-health receipt as covered by a passing code-health receipt on the identical tree in the final Verification. A repository needs no CI job for it, and an uncovered code-health receipt fails CI qualification by name. A round whose code-health requirement was waived (AC3) has its code-health coverage excused by that same waiver, through the existing waived-coverage path."},{"id":"AC6","line":59,"text":"Init. gatereeve code-health init --preset moderate writes the starting config without overwriting existing files:"},{"id":"AC7","line":67,"text":"Doctor. For a repository not opted out, workflow-doctor --repository <path> checks:"},{"id":"AC8","line":74,"text":"GateReeve dogfood. The GateReeve repository contains the AC6 config, adapted to its layout (JS globs over cli/, plugin-src/, apps/desktop/ and ci/; tests excluded). It also has a root tsconfig.json and devDependencies for the tools. The wrapper run on this feature's integration diff against main reports PASS, and that PASS receipt is part of the final acceptance Verification."}],"criteria":[{"criterion":"Regression compare (AC1)","evidence":"node --test output for the code-health suite","fail":"Any case gives the wrong verdict or the wrong advisory split","id":"R1","line":80,"pass":"Automated tests with a fake habit-sensors show: PASS when counts are equal or lower; FAIL when one (file, smell, rule) group increases; pre-existing and suggested findings advisory; line and message changes ignored"},{"criterion":"Scope, renames, base overlay, suppressions and cache (AC1)","evidence":"node --test output","fail":"Any file is mis-scoped, a rename is counted as all-new, the base run uses the base's config, a suppression hides a finding, the checkout changes, or a baseline is reused across different scopes","id":"R2","line":81,"pass":"Tests show: the merge-base diff scope excludes test globs; a renamed file is compared against its base path; the base run sees the head's governed files; both runs get the same explicit file list; added, moved or deleted suppression directives (including a removed eslint-enable) don't hide a new finding; the checkout is untouched; a cached baseline is reused only for an identical scoped file set"},{"criterion":"Output and exit contract (AC1)","evidence":"node --test output","fail":"Any field is missing, an exit code is wrong, or the ordering is wrong","id":"R3","line":82,"pass":"Tests show exit codes 0/1/2, a --json record with every listed field, and coaching text for new findings before the advisory list"},{"criterion":"UNAVAILABLE causes (AC2)","evidence":"node --test output","fail":"Any cause passes or fails instead of being UNAVAILABLE, omits its way forward, or a stale approval blocks a current one","id":"R4","line":83,"pass":"Tests cover each cause (no config; missing sensors, plugin or tool; incomplete-run; parse-error; a sensor crash, non-zero exit or invalid JSON; governed path changed with no matching approval), each giving UNAVAI